Fix in src/app.js, function setTheme. Do not put the suppression class on <html>: the MutationObserver at app.js 4173 watches 'class' on documentElement, so adding and removing a class there would run themeChanged (readTheme, buildDisplay, buildShapeList, re-render) two extra times per switch. Use a class on <body> or an attribute that observer ignores instead.

1. In page.html, add the rule: .no-trans *, .no-trans *::before, .no-trans *::after { transition: none !important; }
2. In setTheme, in this order:
   - document.body.classList.add('no-trans');
   - set or remove data-theme;
   - flush styles with getComputedStyle(document.body).color (or document.body.offsetHeight);
   - document.body.classList.remove('no-trans').
Because the flush computes the new colors while transitions are off, removing the class right away starts none, so no rAF wait is needed. To cover a system theme change while on Auto, do the same add-flush-remove wrap in the matchMedia 'change' path (themeChanged).
